dsh-llamacpp-studio README · What it does：- discovers `llama-server`, model directories and `.gguf` files;
- renders **234 llama-server options** (llama.cpp build 10236) in a category-rail layout, with empty = omitted and preset dropdowns for common values (context 4K–128K, GPU layers, threads, sampling, cache, reasoning budget);
- starts and stops a local llama-server process with readiness probing;
- keeps named configuration profiles and imports/exports JSON;
- streams stdout / stderr / plugin messages into a filterable, copyable, downloadable log;
- opens the llama-server Web UI with one click;
- persists everything in `$DSH_HOME/llamacpp-studio/config.json`.
